-- title:
--   Level automorphisms attached to Γ₀(M') form a finite group
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q \ge 5$, let $M' \ge 1$ be an integer with $q \nmid M'$, and let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell \ge 3$, $\ell \ne q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $q\ell$, and let $\xi \in L$ be a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity. Write $N = (q\ell)^2 M'$ and let $H =$ [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22) $(q\ell)\,M'$ be the kernel of the reduction map $(\mathbb{Z}/N)^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q\ell)^\times$, so that [`CohCarrier.GammaH`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133) $N\,H$ is the congruence subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ consisting of the elements of $\Gamma_0(N)$ whose associated unit lies in $H$, viewed inside $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq L(\!(X)\!)$ (Laurent series over $L$) which is assumed equal to the base change [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) $L$ of the $q$-expansion field [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79) $N\,H \subseteq \mathbb{Q}(\!(X)\!)$, that is, the $L$-subfield of $L(\!(X)\!)$ generated by the coefficientwise images of the elements of that rational $q$-expansion field. The assertion is that there is a subgroup $G$ of the group $\mathrm{Aut}_L(K)$ of $L$-algebra automorphisms of $K$ such that $G$ is finite and, for every $\tau \in \mathrm{Aut}_L(K)$, one has $\tau \in G$ if and only if there exists $\gamma \in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) $L\,(q\ell)\,\xi\,(q\ell)\,N\,H\,\gamma^{-1}\,K\,\tau$ holds. The latter predicate says: for every weight $k \in \mathbb{Z}$, all modular forms $f, g$ of weight $k$ for [`CohCarrier.GammaH`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133) $N\,H$, all integral power series $p_f, p_g$ whose images in $\mathbb{C}[\![X]\!]$ are the $q$-expansions of $f$ and $g$ at width $1$, with the Laurent series of $p_g$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ nonzero, every $x \in K$ whose underlying Laurent series is the coefficientwise image in $L(\!(X)\!)$ of the quotient of the Laurent series of $p_f$ by that of $p_g$, and every ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\xi) = \exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$, the coefficientwise image under $\iota$ of $\tau(x)$, multiplied by the $q$-expansion of $g \mid_k \gamma^{-1,\sharp}$, equals the $q$-expansion of $f \mid_k \gamma^{-1,\sharp}$, where for $\gamma = \begin{pmatrix} a & b \\ c & d\end{pmatrix}$ the matrix $\gamma^{\sharp} =$ [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.conjElemN`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L13) $(q\ell)\,\gamma$ is $\begin{pmatrix} a & b/(q\ell) \\ (q\ell)c & d \end{pmatrix} \in \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$.
--
--   Classically this says that the automorphisms of the function field of $X(\Gamma(q\ell) \cap \Gamma_0(M'))$ over $L$ obtained by pulling back along the conjugates $\gamma^{\sharp}$ of elements $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ constitute the (finite) deck transformation group of the covering $X(\Gamma(q\ell) \cap \Gamma_0(M')) \to X_0(M')$, realised here on the $q$-expansion model $K \subseteq L(\!(X)\!)$. The finiteness of this group is the input to the fixed-field (Artin) argument used in the comparison of chart models over $K$, and it is invoked in the study of the branch primes of the two-chart integral model.
